From: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Jan 2026 23:10:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: raise the hardware A-MSDU limit to 31

The station record limited hardware A-MSDU aggregation to 8
subframes, below the hardware limit of 31 subframes for this chip
family. Use the hardware limit. The A-MSDU length that the peer
advertises still limits each aggregate.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -2024,7 +2024,7 @@ mt7996_mcu_sta_amsdu_tlv(struct mt7996_d
 
 	tlv = mt76_connac_mcu_add_tlv(skb, STA_REC_HW_AMSDU, sizeof(*amsdu));
 	amsdu = (struct sta_rec_amsdu *)tlv;
-	amsdu->max_amsdu_num = 8;
+	amsdu->max_amsdu_num = 31;
 	amsdu->amsdu_en = true;
 	msta_link->wcid.amsdu = true;
 
